      "mmalex/mpe_test": {
        "Author": "mmalex",
        "Date": "2026-07-29",
        "Tags": "midi",
        "name": "MPE Test",
        "description": "This is a test of MPE input and output for Plinky 12. It presents as two large play surfaces, each with a dedicated brightness (CC74) slider which is mapped to Plinky's sample-start / wavetable-position parameter. It accepts normal MIDI on channels 1 and 16 for the two sounds, as well as MPE for up to two zones, supporting per-note pitch bend, brightness, and pressure. It also sends data in MPE format. The mode pads below the play surfaces open the usual synth edit and preset load/save pages, using the same parameter order as Toadstep and Blocks. This is a first test of MPE on Plinky 12, and sets the stage for adding MPE support to other panels. Code is available in the IDE.",
